es\"). See Health\n  Warnings for the residual ambiguity around registration-time run stamping.\n- **All components are in the platform**: architecture context files exist for\n  Dashboard, Model Registry, and Data Science Pipelines (all GA, Konflux\n  onboarded). No repo/license/konflux onboarding chains apply. Documentation is\n  a canonical Jira component (`.context/rhai-components.txt`) used for the\n  docs-authoring epic; it is a content-process component, not a code component\n  to provision, so Rule 20's onboarding chain does not apply to it.\n- **Priority split decision (Step 4)**: HLR-3 (P1, diff view) stays bundled in\n  E001 with HLR-1 (P0, side-by-side view). The diff view shares the same UI\n  surface and the same parameter/metric data as the side-by-side view — it is\n  not \"distinct and deferrable\" per the split test, so splitting would force\n  two epics to build the same surface. Conversely, HLR-2's Dashboard portion\n  (E003) IS split from E001: it is a deferrable feature with independent user\n  value (registry entry point) gated on another team's deliverable (E002), and\n  it consumes — rather than rebuilds — the comparison view.\n- **Priority inheritance**: E001 stays P0 (delivers HLR-1 directly). E002 is P1\n  (enables HLR-2 only). E003 is P1 (HLR-2). E004 is a docs-authoring epic,\n  exempt from priority inheritance; its P1 comes from the strategy frontmatter\n  priority `Major` → P1 per the docs-authoring priority exception (not from\n  HLR-4's P2 level).\n- **Investigations**: the strategy declares \"Open Questions: None\" and\n  contains no pending reviews, conditional ADRs, or risks table. No unknown\n  meets the \"changes which downstream epics exist\" bar, so no Investigation\n  epics were created. The one unclear passage (how the producing-run reference\n  gets stamped at registration time) is an implementation detail resolvable by\n  the Model Registry team within E002's scope, not a flagged genuine unknown.\n\n## Health Warnings\n\n