{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8bbbee811b456f61","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9015\n3\tepic_count: 4\n4\tcritical_path_length: 3\n5\tdecompose_complete: true\n6\trevised: false\n7\ttriage: null\n8\ttriage_rationale: null\n9\t---\n10\t# Decomposition: RHAISTRAT-9015 — Experiment comparison for training and pipeline runs\n11\t\n12\tStrategy status: Refinement Done. Strategy priority: Major. Triage: not\n13\tbelow-threshold (spans three components and three owning teams), not docs-only\n14\t(substantive code changes in Dashboard and Model Registry).\n15\t\n16\t## Epic List\n17\t\n18\t| ID | Title | Type | Team | Priority |\n19\t|----|-------|------|------|----------|\n20\t| RHAISTRAT-9015-E001 | Run comparison view (side-by-side and diff) in the Dashboard | Implementation | RHOAI Dashboard | P0 |\n21\t| RHAISTRAT-9015-E002 | Run lineage on registered model versions in the Model Registry | Implementation | Model Registry | P1 |\n22\t| RHAISTRAT-9015-E003 | Open run comparison from the Model Registry in the Dashboard | Implementation | RHOAI Dashboard | P1 |\n23\t| RHAISTRAT-9015-E004 | Document the run comparison workflow | Implementation (docs-authoring) | RHOAI Documentation | P1 |\n24\t\n25\t## Dependency DAG\n26\t\n27\t```mermaid\n28\tgraph TD\n29\t    E001[\"E001 Run comparison view (P0)\"] --> E003[\"E003 Registry-to-comparison entry (P1)\"]\n30\t    E002[\"E002 Run lineage in Model Registry (P1)\"] --> E003\n31\t    E001 --> E004[\"E004 Documentation (P1)\"]\n32\t    E002 --> E004\n33\t    E003 --> E004\n34\t```\n35\t\n36\t## DAG Justification\n37\t\n38\t| Edge | Rule | Rationale |\n39\t|------|------|-----------|\n40\t| E001 → E003 | Rule 12/13 (framework → consumer) | The registry entry point launches and seeds the comparison view produced by the run comparison work; it builds against that UI capability, so it is serial. |\n41\t| E002 → E003 | Rule 13 (artifact-producing → consuming) | The registry UI entry point renders the producing-run reference that the Model Registry lineage work stores on model versions; without that data artifact there is nothing to surface. |\n42\t| E001 → E004 | Rule 11 (docs blocked by all Implementations) | Documentation must describe the comparison view as built. |\n43\t| E002 → E004 | Rule 11 (docs blocked by all Implementations) | Documentation must describe the registry lineage behavior as built. |\n44\t| E003 → E004 | Rule 11 (docs blocked by all Implementations) | Documentation covers the comparison workflow from both the runs list and the registry, so it needs the registry entry point in place. |\n45\t| No edge E001 ∥ E002 | Rule 14 (different repos, no shared artifacts) | Dashboard and Model Registry are separate repos with independent changes; they run in parallel and converge at E003. |\n46\t\n47\t## HLR Traceability Matrix\n48\t\n49\t| HLR | Priority | Epics | Coverage |\n50\t|-----|----------|-------|----------|\n51\t| HLR-1 (side-by-side comparison of 2+ runs in Dashboard) | P0 | E001 | Full |\n52\t| HLR-2 (registered model versions link back to producing run; comparison openable from registry) | P1 | E002 (lineage storage/exposure), E003 (registry UI entry) | Full |\n53\t| HLR-3 (run diff view highlighting changed parameters and metrics) | P1 | E001 | Full |\n54\t| HLR-4 (documentation of comparison workflow from runs list and registry) | P2 | E004 | Full |\n55\t\n56\tAll HLRs are covered; no orphaned requirements.\n57\t\n58\t## Decomposition Notes\n59\t\n60\t- **Component classification (Step 2)**: Dashboard and Model Registry are\n61\t  active components (code changes) and generate Implementation epics. Data\n62\t  Science Pipelines is classified **passive**: the comparison consumes run\n63\t  parameters and metrics through its existing KFP v2 REST API/SDK interfaces\n64\t  (architecture context: `rhoai-3.0/data-science-pipelines.md`), and the\n65\t  strategy identifies no DSP code change. Passive-component validation is an\n66\t  acceptance criterion on E001 (\"comparison works against Data Science\n67\t  Pipelines runs via existing interfaces; no DSP code changes\"). See Health\n68\t  Warnings for the residual ambiguity around registration-time run stamping.\n69\t- **All components are in the platform**: architecture context files exist for\n70\t  Dashboard, Model Registry, and Data Science Pipelines (all GA, Konflux\n71\t  onboarded). No repo/license/konflux onboarding chains apply. Documentation is\n72\t  a canonical Jira component (`.context/rhai-components.txt`) used for the\n73\t  docs-authoring epic; it is a content-process component, not a code component\n74\t  to provision, so Rule 20's onboarding chain does not apply to it.\n75\t- **Priority split decision (Step 4)**: HLR-3 (P1, diff view) stays bundled in\n76\t  E001 with HLR-1 (P0, side-by-side view). The diff view shares the same UI\n77\t  surface and the same parameter/metric data as the side-by-side view — it is\n78\t  not \"distinct and deferrable\" per the split test, so splitting would force\n79\t  two epics to build the same surface. Conversely, HLR-2's Dashboard portion\n80\t  (E003) IS split from E001: it is a deferrable feature with independent user\n81\t  value (registry entry point) gated on another team's deliverable (E002), and\n82\t  it consumes — rather than rebuilds — the comparison view.\n83\t- **Priority inheritance**: E001 stays P0 (delivers HLR-1 directly). E002 is P1\n84\t  (enables HLR-2 only). E003 is P1 (HLR-2). E004 is a docs-authoring epic,\n85\t  exempt from priority inheritance; its P1 comes from the strategy frontmatter\n86\t  priority `Major` → P1 per the docs-authoring priority exception (not from\n87\t  HLR-4's P2 level).\n88\t- **Investigations**: the strategy declares \"Open Questions: None\" and\n89\t  contains no pending reviews, conditional ADRs, or risks table. No unknown\n90\t  meets the \"changes which downstream epics exist\" bar, so no Investigation\n91\t  epics were created. The one unclear passage (how the producing-run reference\n92\t  gets stamped at registration time) is an implementation detail resolvable by\n93\t  the Model Registry team within E002's scope, not a flagged genuine unknown.\n94\t\n95\t## Health Warnings\n96\t\n97\t1. **Missing strategy sections**: the strategy has no Impacted Teams table, no\n98\t   Dependencies table, no Given/When/Then Acceptance Criteria, and no\n99\t   Non-Functional Requirements. Decomposition proceeded from the HLRs, Affected\n100\t   Components list, and Out-of-Scope list; epic acceptance criteria were\n101\t   derived accordingly. Owning teams were taken from architecture context.\n102\t2. **Data Science Pipelines scope ambiguity**: DSP is listed as an affected\n103\t   component, but no code change is identifiable from the strategy — classified\n104\t   passive (see Decomposition Notes). If capturing the producing-run reference\n105\t   at registration turns out to require pipeline-side/SDK changes in DSP (e.g.\n106\t   stamping run metadata when a pipeline registers a model), a follow-up DSP\n107\t   epic owned by RHOAI Pipelines may be needed; this should be confirmed when\n108\t   the Model Registry lineage work starts. Non-blocking.\n109\t3. **Documentation team inferred**: there is no architecture context file for\n110\t   the Documentation component; the canonical component name from\n111\t   `.context/rhai-components.txt` was used and the owning team was inferred as\n112\t   RHOAI Documentation. Verify assignment before creating the Jira epic.\n113\t4. **Docs priority vs HLR level**: E004 is P1 (docs-authoring exception maps\n114\t   strategy priority Major → P1) even though its source HLR-4 is P2. This is\n115\t   per-rule, not a priority inversion; flagged here so it is not read as one.\n116\t5. **Requirement wording overlap**: the problem statement notes requirements\n117\t   were consolidated from two customer councils with overlapping wording kept.\n