{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-89ca87725dd4c439","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9015-E001\n3\ttitle: Run comparison view (side-by-side and diff) in the Dashboard\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9015\n5\tcomponent: Dashboard\n6\tteam: RHOAI Dashboard\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tai_signals:\n10\t  change_specificity: 0\n11\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n12\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n13\t  existing_foundation: 1\n14\t  open_questions: 1\n15\t  external_dependency: 1\n16\t  human_process_gates: 1\n17\t  repo_access: 1\n18\t  architecture_claims: 0\n19\timplementation_type: null\n20\tdependencies: []\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 6\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Run comparison view (side-by-side and diff) in the Dashboard\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tThis epic delivers the core experiment-comparison capability in the Dashboard:\n34\tdata scientists can select two or more training and pipeline runs and view\n35\ttheir parameters and metrics side by side, and can see a diff that highlights\n36\twhich parameters and metrics changed between two selected runs. This removes\n37\tthe need to export run data to spreadsheets when iterating on experiments and\n38\tcomparing candidate runs for model promotion.\n39\t\n40\t## Scope\n41\t\n42\t- Multi-select of two or more runs from the runs list in the Dashboard.\n43\t- Side-by-side view of parameters and metrics for all selected runs.\n44\t- Diff view that highlights which parameters and metrics differ between two\n45\t  selected runs.\n46\t- Retrieval of run parameters and metrics through the existing Data Science\n47\t  Pipelines interfaces (KFP v2 API) — no Data Science Pipelines code changes\n48\t  are in scope for this work.\n49\t- Comparison stays within a single project; cross-cluster and cross-project\n50\t  comparison are out of scope, as is automatic best-run selection or promotion.\n51\t\n52\t## Acceptance Criteria\n53\t\n54\t- Given a project containing two or more runs, when the user selects them and\n55\t  opens the comparison, then the parameters and metrics of all selected runs\n56\t  are displayed side by side.\n57\t- Given two selected runs, when the user opens the diff view, then parameters\n58\t  and metrics that changed between the two runs are highlighted, and unchanged\n59\t  values are distinguishable from changed ones.\n60\t- The comparison works against runs produced by Data Science Pipelines using\n61\t  its existing run interfaces, with no Data Science Pipelines code changes\n62\t  (passive-component validation).\n63\t- Comparison is scoped to runs within a single project; no cross-project or\n64\t  cross-cluster comparison is offered.\n65\t\n66\t## HLR Traceability\n67\t\n68\t- HLR-1 (P0): users can select two or more runs and view their parameters and\n69\t  metrics side by side in the Dashboard.\n70\t- HLR-3 (P1): run diff view highlighting which parameters and metrics changed\n71\t  between two selected runs.\n72\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-86e37f882db42d7a","agent_id":"a3c147d88e27d77d5","session_id":"a66a1624-e5ea-4bd7-921c-fe9a2fc3883b","uuid":"71cc2974-8f2e-4c35-b265-96d3c1077352","timestamp":"2026-10-21T17:11:01.830Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-89ca87725dd4c439","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-9015 decomposition"}
