{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-847098252bf02678","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9015-E002\n3\ttitle: Run lineage on registered model versions in the Model Registry\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9015\n5\tcomponent: Model Registry\n6\tteam: Model Registry\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tai_signals:\n10\t  change_specificity: 0\n11\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n12\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n13\t  existing_foundation: 1\n14\t  open_questions: 1\n15\t  external_dependency: 0\n16\t  human_process_gates: 1\n17\t  repo_access: 1\n18\t  architecture_claims: 0\n19\timplementation_type: null\n20\tdependencies: []\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 6\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Run lineage on registered model versions in the Model Registry\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tThis epic makes registered model versions carry a reference to the run that\n34\tproduced them, so that any consumer of the Model Registry can resolve the\n35\ttraining/pipeline lineage of a model version. It uses the Model Registry's\n36\texisting extension point for structured metadata on model versions (custom\n37\tproperties), keeping the change within established registry patterns.\n38\t\n39\t## Scope\n40\t\n41\t- Capture a producing-run reference on registered model versions at\n42\t  registration time. The reference must be sufficient to resolve the run\n43\t  (project and run identity). Specific property naming and exact capture\n44\t  mechanism are implementation decisions for the Model Registry team within\n45\t  the custom-properties extension point.\n46\t- Ensure registration flows can supply the run reference, including\n47\t  registration performed from within a pipeline run.\n48\t- Expose the run reference on model versions through the Model Registry REST\n49\t  API so clients (such as the Dashboard) can read it.\n50\t- Registration flows that have no run reference continue to work; the lineage\n51\t  link is additive and optional.\n52\t\n53\t## Acceptance Criteria\n54\t\n55\t- Given a model version registered from a known run, the stored model version\n56\t  carries a reference that resolves to that run.\n57\t- The producing-run reference is readable through the Model Registry REST API\n58\t  on the model version entity.\n59\t- Existing registration flows without a run reference succeed unchanged\n60\t  (backwards compatible; the link is optional metadata).\n61\t\n62\t## HLR Traceability\n63\t\n64\t- HLR-2 (P1, storage and exposure side): registered model versions link back\n65\t  to the run that produced them.\n66\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8df6ea497e5d22e3","agent_id":"ac1a4a8071d915878","session_id":"a66a1624-e5ea-4bd7-921c-fe9a2fc3883b","uuid":"606631a2-7174-4041-8b92-3e4378f0facf","timestamp":"2026-10-21T17:14:01.749Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-847098252bf02678","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9015 decomposition"}
