{"type":"system","subtype":"task_notification","task_id":"aaaa44161d60520c4","run_id":"0mvidk1nd-948e1629","tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ab5e0f38c6e8aeee","status":"completed","output_file":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-private-var-folders-h5-l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn-T-epic-RHAISTRAT-9015-7atpc68d/a66a1624-e5ea-4bd7-921c-fe9a2fc3883b/tasks/aaaa44161d60520c4.output","summary":"Revision complete for RHAISTRAT-9015. Both review issues were fixed:\n\n1. **HLR-3 priority collapse (major)**: Split the run diff view out of the P0 epic. `RHAISTRAT-9015-E001` is now \"Run comparison view (side-by-side) in the Dashboard\" (P0, HLR-1 only — diff scope, AC, and traceability removed). Created new `RHAISTRAT-9015-E005` \"Run diff view in the Dashboard\" (P1, HLR-3, Dashboard/RHOAI Dashboard) depending on E001 (framework→consumer: it renders within the comparison surface), with the shared-surface concern encoded as a coordination/AC gate. E004 (docs) now also depends on E005 per the Rule 11 docs edge since it documents the diff view. New `RHAISTRAT-9015-E005-ai-signals.md` rationale file added.\n2. **E002 external_dependency (minor)**: Changed `ai_signals.external_dependency` from 0 to 1 and rewrote the rationale in `RHAISTRAT-9015-E002-ai-signals.md` (change stays within the documented custom-properties extension point; upstream coordination risk was speculative). `ai_implementability`/`ai_implementability_score` left untouched per instructions.\n\nThe decomposition summary (`artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9015-decomposition.md`) was updated: epic list (5 rows), mermaid DAG with the two new edges, DAG justification rows, HLR-3 → E005 in the traceability matrix, rewritten priority-split decision and priority-inheritance notes, and Health Warning 6 rewritten as a shared-surface coordination note. Frontmatter set to `revised=true epic_count=5 critical_path_length=3`.\n\nVerification passed: all 5 epic files validate against the epic-task schema, all dependencies resolve to existing