{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-acf936983860685a","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9015-E001\n3\ttitle: Run comparison view (side-by-side) in the Dashboard\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9015\n5\tcomponent: Dashboard\n6\tteam: RHOAI Dashboard\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tai_signals:\n10\t  change_specificity: 0\n11\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n12\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n13\t  existing_foundation: 1\n14\t  open_questions: 1\n15\t  external_dependency: 1\n16\t  human_process_gates: 1\n17\t  repo_access: 1\n18\t  architecture_claims: 0\n19\timplementation_type: null\n20\tdependencies: []\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 6\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Run comparison view (side-by-side) in the Dashboard\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tThis epic delivers the core experiment-comparison capability in the Dashboard:\n34\tdata scientists can select two or more training and pipeline runs and view\n35\ttheir parameters and metrics side by side. This removes the need to export run\n36\tdata to spreadsheets when iterating on experiments and comparing candidate\n37\truns for model promotion. The run diff view (highlighting changed parameters\n38\tand metrics between two runs) is a separate deferrable feature tracked in its\n39\town epic; this epic delivers only the side-by-side comparison surface.\n40\t\n41\t## Scope\n42\t\n43\t- Multi-select of two or more runs from the runs list in the Dashboard.\n44\t- Side-by-side view of parameters and metrics for all selected runs.\n45\t- Retrieval of run parameters and metrics through the existing Data Science\n46\t  Pipelines interfaces (KFP v2 API) — no Data Science Pipelines code changes\n47\t  are in scope for this work.\n48\t- Comparison stays within a single project; cross-cluster and cross-project\n49\t  comparison are out of scope, as is automatic best-run selection or promotion.\n50\t\n51\t## Acceptance Criteria\n52\t\n53\t- Given a project containing two or more runs, when the user selects them and\n54\t  opens the comparison, then the parameters and metrics of all selected runs\n55\t  are displayed side by side.\n56\t- The comparison works against runs produced by Data Science Pipelines using\n57\t  its existing run interfaces, with no Data Science Pipelines code changes\n58\t  (passive-component validation).\n59\t- Comparison is scoped to runs within a single project; no cross-project or\n60\t  cross-cluster comparison is offered.\n61\t\n62\t## HLR Traceability\n63\t\n64\t- HLR-1 (P0): users can select two or more runs and view their parameters and\n65\t  metrics side by side in the Dashboard.\n66\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b69241d1f68fb7e1","agent_id":"a4882fb7b245e47bb","session_id":"a66a1624-e5ea-4bd7-921c-fe9a2fc3883b","uuid":"71a0f323-03a7-4cc6-8191-d7b1e1aa6754","timestamp":"2026-10-21T17:21:42.465Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-acf936983860685a","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review after second revision"}
